# Backend API URL
# Dev: leave empty → defaults to http://localhost:8000
# Prod: set to your Railway backend URL
VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.up.railway.app

# Stripe Price IDs are NOT read from environment variables — they never were:
# this file used to document REACT_APP_STRIPE_* names (Create React App's
# prefix), but this app is built with Vite, which only exposes VITE_*
# variables to client code. That config was dead, silently ignored.
# The real, live Price IDs are hardcoded in
# frontend-react/src/pages/LandingPage.tsx (PRICE_IDS_YOUTUBE,
# PRICE_IDS_TWITCH, PRICE_IDS_COMBO) — edit them there when a plan's Stripe
# Price ID changes. This is safe: Price IDs are meant to be public, used
# client-side only to start a Stripe Checkout session.